B.aaM=s(["al-kahf","kahf","friday"],t.s)
B.aQg=new A.aR(B.aaM,"The Prophet \ufdfa said: \u201cWhoever reads Surah Al-Kahf on Friday, a light will shine for him between the two Fridays.\u201d (al-Bayhaqi, classed sahih). Its first ten verses are also a protection from the trial of the Dajjal (Sahih Muslim).")
B.ah7=s(["anxiety","anxious","worry","worried","stress","grief"],t.s)
B.aPI=new A.aR(B.ah7,"\u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f\u0645\u064e\u0651 \u0625\u0650\u0646\u0650\u0651\u064a \u0623\u064e\u0639\u064f\u0648\u0630\u064f \u0628\u0650\u0643\u064e \u0645\u0650\u0646\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0647\u064e\u0645\u0650\u0651 \u0648\u064e\u0627\u0644\u0652\u062d\u064e\u0632\u064e\u0646\u0650 \u2014 \u201cO Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, from incapacity and laziness, from cowardice and miserliness, from the burden of debt and from being overpowered by men.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 6369). You will also find it in your Morning Adhkar set.")
B.aoF=s(["witr"],t.s)
B.aQ7=new A.aR(B.aoF,"Witr is prayed after \u2018Isha until Fajr, as an odd number of rak'ahs \u2014 most simply one. \u201cAllah is Witr (One) and loves witr.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 990). After ruku\u2018 you may recite Qunut: \u201cAllahumma ihdini fiman hadayt\u2026\u201d (Sunan Abu Dawood 1425).")
B.aks=s(["morning adhkar","adhkar","dhikr","remembrance"],t.s)
B.aQb=new A.aR(B.aks,"Your Dhikr & Du'a screen holds the morning, evening, and after-prayer sets from Hisn al-Muslim with meanings. The Prophet \ufdfa said the morning and evening adhkar protect the one who says them (Sunan Abu Dawood 5088). Open it from Home and tap the counters as you recite.")
B.ah5=s(["ramadan","fasting","fast","sawm","suhoor","iftar"],t.s)
B.aQ3=new A.aR(B.ah5,"Fasting Ramadan is the fourth pillar of Islam (Qur'an 2:183-185). \u201cWhoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and hope for reward, his past sins are forgiven.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 38). Take suhoor \u2014 \u201cin suhoor there is blessing\u201d (Bukhari 1923) \u2014 and check the Islamic Calendar screen for this year's dates.")
B.apn=s(["zakat","charity","sadaqah"],t.s)
B.aPg=new A.aR(B.apn,"Zakat is the third pillar \u2014 2.5% of qualifying wealth held a lunar year above the nisab. \u201cWhoever pays it seeking reward\u2026\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 1395). The Zakat screen in Ar-Rayaan calculates it for you step by step.")
B.ajq=s(["prayer time","prayer times","salah times","namaz time"],t.s)
B.aP2=new A.aR(B.ajq,"Your Prayer Times screen calculates today's schedule right on your device \u2014 tap GPS or choose your city, and turn on the bell next to any prayer to be alerted when its time arrives.")
B.acA=s(["how do i pray","how to pray","salah","pray witr"],t.s)
B.aPt=new A.aR(B.acA,"Prayer is the second pillar. \u201cPray as you have seen me pray.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 631). Five daily prayers are obligatory; the Prophet's \ufdfa complete method is recorded across the six books \u2014 Shaykh Saqib Iqbal's channel (in Our Sources) walks through it beautifully, step by step.")
B.al7=s(["quran","qur'an","recite","recitation"],t.s)
B.aPs=new A.aR(B.al7,"The Qur'an screen holds all 114 surahs \u2014 tap any ayah to hear recitation by Shaykh Mishary Rashid Alafasy. \u201cThe best of you are those who learn the Qur'an and teach it.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 5027).")
B.a8I=s(["dua for anxiety","du'a","dua","supplication"],t.s)
B.aOX=new A.aR(B.a8I,"Du'a is worship itself (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3372). For a need, begin with praise of Allah and salawat on the Prophet \ufdfa, then ask with certainty. Your Dhikr & Du'a screen carries the authentic daily supplications with their meanings.")
B.akw=s(["eid"],t.s)
B.aPe=new A.aR(B.akw,"The two Eids are days of prayer, takbir, and celebration (Sahih al-Bukhari 950-956). Eid al-Fitr follows Ramadan; Eid al-Adha falls on 10 Dhul-Hijjah, the day after Arafah. Exact dates for this year are on the Islamic Calendar screen.")
B.aeK=s(["sources","authentic","hadith book","sihah","bukhari"],t.s)
B.aPP=new A.aR(B.aeK,"Ar-Rayaan builds only on the Qur'an and the Sihah Sitta \u2014 the six authentic books: Sahih al-Bukhari, Sahih Muslim, Sunan Abu Dawood, Jami' at-Tirmidhi, Sunan an-Nasa'i, and Sunan Ibn Majah \u2014 with Shaykh Muhammad Saqib Iqbal's channel for guided learning. See the full list on the Our Sources screen.")
B.alC=s(["hajj","umrah","pilgrimage"],t.s)
B.aPC=new A.aR(B.alC,"Hajj is the fifth pillar, owed once in a lifetime by those able (Qur'an 3:97). \u201cAn accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 1773). Umrah can be performed any time of year.")
B.apc=s(["tahajjud","night prayer","qiyam"],t.s)
B.aPK=new A.aR(B.apc,"The night prayer is the best prayer after the obligatory ones (Sahih Muslim 1163). The last third of the night is a special time for du'a \u2014 your Prayer Times screen shows tonight's window.")
B.al5=s(["forgive","repent","tawbah","sin"],t.s)
B.aP8=new A.aR(B.al5,"Allah says: \u201cDo not despair of Allah's mercy; indeed Allah forgives all sins.\u201d (Qur'an 39:53). The Prophet \ufdfa said: \u201cEvery son of Adam sins, and the best of sinners are those who repent.\u201d (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 2499, sahih). The door is open \u2014 walk through it.")
B.amH=s(["mother","father","parents"],t.s)
B.aOI=new A.aR(B.amH,"\u201cParadise lies beneath the feet of mothers.\u201d (Sunan an-Nasa'i 3104, sahih). The Prophet \ufdfa was asked who most deserves good companionship: \u201cYour mother\u201d \u2014 three times \u2014 \u201cthen your father.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 5971).")
B.alS=s(["istighfar","sayyid"],t.s)
B.aP4=new A.aR(B.alS,"Sayyid al-Istighfar is the master supplication for forgiveness \u2014 it opens your Morning Adhkar set. Whoever says it with conviction in the morning and dies that day enters Paradise (Sahih al-Bukhari 6306).")
B.aoa=s(["patience","sabr","hardship","difficult","trial"],t.s)
B.aPb=new A.aR(B.aoa,"\u201cIndeed, Allah is with the patient.\u201d (Qur'an 2:153). \u201cAmazing is the affair of the believer: all of it is good for him \u2014 gratitude in ease, patience in hardship.\u201d (Sahih Muslim 2999). This too shall pass, and nothing is wasted with Him.")
B.akl=s(["name of allah","names of allah","99"],t.s)
B.aPZ=new A.aR(B.akl,"\u201cAllah has ninety-nine names; whoever preserves them enters Paradise.\u201d (Sahih al-Bukhari 2736). Begin with Ar-Rahman \u2014 the Most Merciful \u2014 the name He opens His Book with.")
B.a98=s(["salaam","salam","assalamu","wa alaikum","hello","hey "],t.s)
B.aPA=new A.aR(B.a98,"Wa alaikum as-salam wa rahmatullah - and upon you be peace and mercy. How may I walk beside you today? Ask me about worship, the Qur'an, this app, or simply talk.")
B.ajx=s(["how are you","how do you feel"],t.s)
B.aQf=new A.aR(B.ajx,"Alhamdulillah - all praise belongs to Allah. More importantly: how are YOU? If something weighs on your heart, I can make du'a with you, or take you to Sakina for stillness.")
B.a9a=s(["who are you","your name","your hadi"],t.s)
B.aOJ=new A.aR(B.a9a,"I am Hadi - \"the guide\" - your companion inside Ar-Rayaan. I answer from the Qur'an and the Sihah Sitta: Sahih al-Bukhari, Sahih Muslim, Sunan Abu Dawood, Jami' at-Tirmidhi, Sunan an-Nasa'i, and Sunan Ibn Majah - and I know every room of this app. I would rather say \"I don't know\" than invent. My sister-teacher Wasia runs the letter school.")
B.an4=s(["who is wasia","what is wasia"],t.s)
B.aPV=new A.aR(B.an4,"Wasia is the AI teacher of the Wasia Academy - the letter school built with love. She teaches the Arabic alphabet, reads with the child, and speaks in three voices: student, parent, and a Teachers' Corner for parents. Shall I take you there?\n[GO:/academy/gate]")
B.ao5=s(["thank","jazak","shukran","thanks"],t.s)
B.aPw=new A.aR(B.ao5,"Wa iyyakum - and you likewise, many times over. May Allah accept from you. I am here whenever you need me.")
B.afn=s(["what can you do","what do you do","features","guide me"],t.s)
B.aPO=new A.aR(B.afn,"Three things, always: (1) answer from the Qur'an and the Sihah Sitta - verses, du'as, rulings, with sources; (2) teach you this app room by room - prayer times, Qur'an, stories, zakat, games; (3) walk you there myself - just say \"take me to...\" and I will. What shall we begin with?")
B.amf=s(["quran screen","read the quran","recitation screen","open quran"],t.s)
B.aPT=new A.aR(B.amf,"Opening the Qur'an - tap any ayah to hear Shaykh Mishary Rashid Alafasy recite.\n[GO:/quran]")
B.amx=s(["prayer times screen","prayer screen","salah times screen"],t.s)
B.aOL=new A.aR(B.amx,"Opening your Prayer Times - tap the bell beside any prayer to be alerted when its time arrives.\n[GO:/prayer]")
B.aiK=s(["adhkar screen","dhikr screen","dua screen","du'a screen"],t.s)
B.aQa=new A.aR(B.aiK,"Opening Dhikr & Du'a - the Hisn al-Muslim sets with counters and meanings.\n[GO:/adhkar]")
B.a9X=s(["zakat screen","zakat calculator"],t.s)
B.aOG=new A.aR(B.a9X,"Opening the Zakat calculator - it walks you through nisab and rates step by step.\n[GO:/zakat]")
B.ad4=s(["stories screen","story screen","prophets screen"],t.s)
B.aPJ=new A.aR(B.ad4,"Opening Stories - Prophets, Women, Seerah, Companions, duas and khutbahs. Inside any story you can ask me about it as you read.\n[GO:/stories]")
B.aez=s(["search screen","find anything","find screen"],t.s)
B.aP9=new A.aR(B.aez,"Opening Find Anything - one search across every shelf of the app.\n[GO:/search]")
B.akZ=s(["games screen","game screen"],t.s)
B.aPB=new A.aR(B.akZ,"Opening Games - Shatranj, Ludo, Trivia, and the 99 Names.\n[GO:/games]")
B.aef=s(["99 names screen","names screen","names of allah screen"],t.s)
B.aQ6=new A.aR(B.aef,'Opening the 99 Names - learn them one by one; "whoever preserves them enters Paradise."\n[GO:/games/names99]')
B.afj=s(["hadith screen","forty hadith","nawawi screen"],t.s)
B.aOR=new A.aR(B.afj,"Opening the Forty Hadith of an-Nawawi, Arabic with meanings.\n[GO:/hadith]")
B.a9g=s(["qibla screen","find qibla","qibla direction","face qibla"],t.s)
B.aPx=new A.aR(B.a9g,"Opening Qibla - hold your phone flat and it points you to the Ka'bah.\n[GO:/qibla]")
B.anq=s(["calendar screen","islamic calendar","ramadan dates","eid dates"],t.s)
B.aPn=new A.aR(B.anq,"Opening the Islamic Calendar - this year's months, Ramadan and Eid dates.\n[GO:/calendar]")
B.amR=s(["finance screen","stocks screen","trading screen","halal stocks"],t.s)
B.aP3=new A.aR(B.amR,"Opening Tayyib Finance - the halal stock screener and a paper trading floor to practice on.\n[GO:/finance]")
B.aoX=s(["academy screen","school screen","letters screen","alphabet"],t.s)
B.aOV=new A.aR(B.aoX,"Opening Wasia Academy - where children learn the Arabic letters with Wasia.\n[GO:/academy/gate]")
B.alJ=s(["feelings screen","heart screen"],t.s)
B.aPD=new A.aR(B.alJ,"Opening For Your Heart - a gentle feelings guide with a du'a for every state.\n[GO:/feelings]")
B.akj=s(["sakina","comfort screen","peace screen"],t.s)
B.aPj=new A.aR(B.akj,"Opening Sakina - a page of stillness for when the heart is heavy.\n[GO:/sakina]")
B.abZ=s(["family tree screen","messengers screen"],t.s)
B.aPy=new A.aR(B.abZ,"Opening the Messengers' family tree - from Adam to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon them all).\n[GO:/family-tree]")
B.ajc=s(["share screen","cards screen","verse cards"],t.s)
B.aOD=new A.aR(B.ajc,"Opening verse cards - share an ayah with someone you love.\n[GO:/share]")
B.a8P=s(["sources screen","our sources"],t.s)
B.aQi=new A.aR(B.a8P,"Opening Our Sources - every authority this app builds on.\n[GO:/sources]")
B.adX=s(["settings screen","api key","apikey","add a key"],t.s)
B.aPG=new A.aR(B.adX,"Opening Settings - in Hadi's section you can add your free API key so I can reason further; without one I still answer from the curated shelf.\n[GO:/settings]")
B.adg=s(["masajid","masjid","mosque","halal food","restaurants"],t.s)
B.aQ2=new A.aR(B.adg,"Opening Masajid & Halal - prayer spaces and halal food near you.\n[GO:/masajid]")
B.a7S=s(["shahada","testimony","declaration of faith"],t.s)
B.aPu=new A.aR(B.a7S,'The testimony: "La ilaha illallah, Muhammadur rasulullah" - there is no god worthy of worship but Allah, and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. The first pillar; on it everything stands.')
B.adE=s(["pillars of islam","five pillars"],t.s)
B.aPL=new A.aR(B.adE,"The five pillars: the testimony of faith, the five daily prayers, zakat, the fast of Ramadan, and Hajj for those able - each established in the Qur'an and the Sunnah.")
B.aoI=s(["wudu","ablution"],t.s)
B.aPE=new A.aR(B.aoI,'Wudu is the purification before prayer: wash the face, hands to the elbows, wipe head and ears, wash the feet - with intention and in order. "Allah does not accept prayer without purification." (Sahih Muslim 224).')
B.a7z=s(["grave","after death","hereafter"],t.s)
B.aPf=new A.aR(B.a7z,'The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: "Remember often the destroyer of pleasures - death." (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 2307). Live each prayer as if it were your last; the grave is a garden from Paradise or a pit from the Fire - and its morning is near.')
B.amp=s(["morning adhkar","evening adhkar","morning dua","evening dua","morning remembrance","evening remembrance"],t.s)
B.aOS=new A.aR(B.amp,'The morning and evening adhkar are the shield of the day: Ayat al-Kursi, the three Quls, "Raditu billahi rabba..." - whoever says them morning and evening is sufficed. They live in your Dhikr & Du\'a sets with counters and meanings.')
B.ahF=s(["before eating","after eating","eating dua","food dua","eat dua"],t.s)
B.aOZ=new A.aR(B.ahF,'Before eating: "Bismillah" - and if you forget, say "Bismillahi awwalahu wa akhirahu". After: "Alhamdulillahilladhi at\'amana wa saqana wa ja\'alana muslimin" - all praise to Allah who fed us, gave us drink, and made us Muslims. (Abu Dawood 3761, 3201)')
B.aeJ=s(["dua for parents","my parents","parents","mother dua","father dua"],t.s)
B.aOC=new A.aR(B.aeJ,"The Qur'an itself teaches the du'a: \"Rabbir hamhumaa kamaa rabbayaani saghira\" - My Lord, have mercy on them as they raised me when I was small (Al-Isra 24). Say it after every prayer; it is among the most beloved of speech.")
B.alb=s(["dua for the sick","someone sick","visiting the sick","ill dua","cure dua"],t.s)
B.aON=new A.aR(B.alb,'For the sick: place your hand where it hurts and say "Bismillah" three times, then "As\'alullah al-\'Azim Rabbal-\'arshil-azim an yashfiyak" - I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to cure you - seven times. (Sahih al-Bukhari 5675). And visiting the sick is an expiation: its fruits ripen in Paradise. (Bukhari 5402)')
B.afs=s(["anxious","anxiety","worried","worry","depressed","overwhelmed","scared","afraid"],t.s)
B.aP0=new A.aR(B.afs,'For a heavy heart: "Hasbunallahu wa ni\'mal wakeel" - Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best Disposer of affairs (Al-Imran 173) - the words of Ibrahim and our Prophet in distress. And the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: "There is no worry or grief for the servant who, in hardship, says: Ya Hayyu ya Qayyum, bi-rahmatika astagheeth." (Sunan Ibn Majah 3881). Sakina is in this app for you too.')
B.ahG=s(["niyyah","intention","why do we","actions are"],t.s)
B.aPa=new A.aR(B.ahG,'"Actions are only by intentions, and every person shall have what he intended." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1 - the very first hadith). The reward of an act lives in its intention: prayer for showing off is empty, and sweeping a floor for Allah is worship.')
B.act=s(["mercy","be kind","kindness","gentle","compassion"],t.s)
B.aPd=new A.aR(B.act,'"The merciful are shown mercy by Ar-Rahman. Be merciful to those on earth, and the One above the heavens will be merciful to you." (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 1924). "He who does not show mercy will not be shown mercy." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6013). Kindness - rifq - beautifies everything it touches.')
B.aku=s(["neighbor","neighbour","next door"],t.s)
B.aPU=new A.aR(B.aku,"Jibreel kept advising the Prophet about the neighbor until he thought he would make him an heir: the neighbor has a right almost of kinship. (Sahih al-Bukhari 6015) Good neighborhood - guarding dignity, sharing food, soft greetings - is faith in daily dress.")
B.afO=s(["gossip","backbite","speak good","talk bad","rumors"],t.s)
B.aQ8=new A.aR(B.afO,'"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6018). Backbiting - mentioning your brother with what he dislikes - is described in the Qur\'an as eating the flesh of a dead brother (Al-Hujurat 12). If speech is not good, silence is worship.')
B.am4=s(["sadaqah","charity","give money","donate"],t.s)
B.aOE=new A.aR(B.am4,'"Charity does not decrease wealth." (Sahih Muslim 2588). "Your smile in your brother\'s face is charity; removing harm from the path is charity." (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 1956). The zakat calculator in this app handles the obligatory share; beyond it, even half a date shields against the Fire. (Bukhari 5049)')
B.ahw=s(["tawbah","repent","repentance","forgiveness","forgive me","sinned"],t.s)
B.aQe=new A.aR(B.ahw,'Allah says: "Despair not of the mercy of Allah; indeed Allah forgives all sins" (Az-Zumar 53). The Prophet said: "By the One in Whose hand is my soul, if you did not sin, Allah would replace you with people who sin and seek forgiveness - and He would forgive them." (Sahih Muslim 2749). Repentance: leave the sin, regret it, resolve not to return - and restore rights if anyone was wronged.')
B.agQ=s(["hajj","pilgrimage","makkah trip"],t.s)
B.aPi=new A.aR(B.agQ,'Hajj, the fifth pillar, is owed once in a lifetime by whoever can find a way: "And to Allah is a duty upon mankind - the pilgrimage of the House - for whoever can make the way" (Al-Imran 97). "An accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1521). Its rites gather at the Ka\'bah, Arafat, Muzdalifah, and Mina across Dhul-Hijjah.')
B.aga=s(["umrah","minor pilgrimage","omra"],t.s)
B.aPr=new A.aR(B.aga,"Umrah is the shorter pilgrimage, performable any time of year: ihram, tawaf of the Ka'bah, sa'i between Safa and Marwah, and shaving or shortening the hair. The Prophet said an Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj with him in reward. (Sahih al-Bukhari 1782)")
B.amP=s(["tahajjud","night prayer","qiyam","pray at night"],t.s)
B.aPX=new A.aR(B.amP,'"The best prayer after the obligatory prayers is the night prayer." (Sahih Muslim 1163). Tahajjud is prayed after sleeping a portion of the night, in units of two: "Their sides forsake their beds, calling their Lord in fear and hope" (As-Sajdah 16). Start with two rak\'ah before Fajr; Allah descends to the lowest heaven asking who is calling upon Him. (Bukhari 1145)')
B.aeV=s(["istikhara","decision dua","should i do","big decision","choice dua"],t.s)
B.aOW=new A.aR(B.aeV,'For any matter - marriage, a job, a move - pray two units of non-obligatory prayer, then the du\'a of istikhara taught by the Prophet himself: "Allahumma inni astakhiruka bi-\'ilmik..." - O Allah, I seek Your choice by Your knowledge... Then choose what feels settled in your heart, for the Prophet said: "If one of you intends a matter, let him pray two rak\'ah." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1162)')
B.anD=s(["laylatul qadr","night of decree","qadr","best night","odd nights"],t.s)
B.aP1=new A.aR(B.anD,'Laylatul Qadr, in the last ten nights of Ramadan - in the odd nights, the 21st, 23rd, 25th, 27th, 29th: "Better than a thousand months" (Al-Qadr 3). Seek it in the odd nights: stand, recite, ask - "There is no night in which the servants descend more numerous..." (Bukhari 2017). What would you do with 83 years of worship in one night?')
B.ad5=s(["breaking fast","iftar dua","iftar","end of fast"],t.s)
B.aPN=new A.aR(B.ad5,"At iftar, before eating, say: \"Dhahaba al-zama'u wabtallat al-urooqu wa thabata al-ajru in sha Allah\" - The thirst is gone, the veins are moistened, and the reward is fixed, if Allah wills. (Sunan Abu Dawood 2357). The fasting person has a du'a at the moment of breaking that is not rejected. (Ibn Majah 1753)")
B.ajL=s(["durood","salawat","bless the prophet","blessings on the prophet"],t.s)
B.aPM=new A.aR(B.ajL,'"Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten upon him." (Sahih Muslim 408). The least of it: "Allahumma salli \'ala Muhammad" - O Allah, send Your peace and blessings upon Muhammad. It is the signature of love: your prayer is not complete without it.')
B.ago=s(["spread salam","say salam","greeting islam","how to greet"],t.s)
B.aPH=new A.aR(B.ago,'"Spread salam among yourselves." (Sahih al-Bukhari 28). The greeting of Islam - "As-salamu alaikum warahmatullah" - carries three levels: peace, then mercy, then Allah\'s blessings; add them all, for each raises the giver a degree and wipes a sin.')
B.aiu=s(["seeking knowledge","learn islam","study","ilm","become a scholar"],t.s)
B.aQ1=new A.aR(B.aiu,'"Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim." (Sunan Ibn Majah 224 - the chain is debated, but the meaning is carried by the whole religion). The best of you, said the Prophet, are those who learn the Qur\'an and teach it. (Sahih al-Bukhari 5027). Ten minutes daily outlasts a weekend of regret.')
B.aex=s(["plant a tree","small deeds","tiny good deed","good deeds small"],t.s)
B.aPm=new A.aR(B.aex,'"If a Muslim plants a tree, or sows a crop, and a bird or a person or an animal eats of it, it is counted as charity for him." (Sahih al-Bukhari 2320). And the man who gave a thirsty dog water - Allah thanked him and forgave him. (Bukhari 3467) No good deed is too small for His scale.')
B.anI=s(["names on the day of judgment","resurrection names","called by name","name on judgment day"],t.s)
B.aPF=new A.aR(B.anI,'The Prophet said: "You will be called on the Day of Resurrection by your names and the names of your fathers, so make your names beautiful." (Sunan Abu Dawood 4948) - a name carried with goodness becomes a light.')
B.aiX=s(["sick suffering","going through hardship","why me","afflicted","trials"],t.s)
B.aPp=new A.aR(B.aiX,'The Prophet said: "When Allah wills good for a slave, He afflicts him." (Sahih al-Bukhari 5645) - and "No fatigue, illness, anxiety, sorrow, harm or sadness touches a Muslim, even a thorn, but Allah expiates by it." (Bukhari 5641). The pain you did not choose becomes the expiation you did not earn.')
B.amN=s(["leaving home","entering home","go out","come back home","exit the house"],t.s)
B.aPY=new A.aR(B.amN,'Leaving home: "Bismillahi, tawakkaltu \'alallah, la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah" - In Allah\'s name, I trust in Allah; there is no might nor power except with Allah - it is said to you: you are guided, sufficed, and protected. (Sunan Abu Dawood 5095). Entering home: greet with salam, say "Bismillah" as you enter, and "Allahumma inni as\'aluka khayral mawla...". (Muslim 2018)')
B.amm=s(["travel dua","going on a trip","road trip dua","flying dua","journey dua","travel","trip"],t.s)
B.aQh=new A.aR(B.amm,'Before and during travel: "Subhanalladhi sakhkhara lana hadha wa ma kunna lahu muqrinin, wa inna ila rabbina lamunqalibun" - Glory to Him who subjected this to us, and we could never have accomplished it ourselves - and indeed, to our Lord we will return. (Sahih Muslim 1342). Shorten the four-unit prayers when you travel beyond the city.')
B.amz=s(["sneezing","sneeze","alhamdulillah sneeze","bless sneeze"],t.s)
B.aQ5=new A.aR(B.amz,'When someone sneezes and praises Allah ("Alhamdulillah"), say "Yarhamukumullah" - may Allah have mercy on you. The sneezer replies "Yahdikumullah..." (Sahih al-Bukhari 6224). A learned custom: sneeze in privacy, praise Allah, and be answered with mercy.')
B.aaG=s(["dream interpretation","had a dream","strange dream","bad dream","nightmare","dream"],t.s)
B.aPh=new A.aR(B.aaG,"The Prophet taught: the righteous dream is from Allah - thank Him and tell whom you love; the distressing dream is from shaytan - seek refuge in Allah from its evil, do not narrate it, and it will not harm you. Spit lightly to your left three times. (Sahih al-Bukhari 3292). Not every dream carries a meaning - most are what the daytime leaves behind.")
B.ahX=s(["evil eye","hasad","envy","someone envied me","nazr","ruqyah","protect my children"],t.s)
B.aOQ=new A.aR(B.ahX,'The Prophet said: "The evil eye is real and can put a man in the grave and a camel into the cooking pot." (Sahih Muslim 2188). The shield: Ayat al-Kursi, the three Quls said morning and evening, and "la ilaha illallah wahdahu la sharika lah..." for one hundred mornings. For ruqyah, the greatest of it is Al-Fatiha - the Prophet once healed a tribesman with it and was paid thirty sheep. (Bukhari 5748)')
B.aoT=s(["marriage proposal","getting married","choosing spouse","marry someone","marriage advice","marry","marriage"],t.s)
B.aOM=new A.aR(B.aoT,"The Prophet's counsel: \"When someone whose religion and character pleases you proposes to you, then marry him. If you do not, there will be corruption in the land and widespread evil.\" (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 1085). Religion first - beauty and wealth open like flowers and close like them; faith is the root that stays.")
B.aeD=s(["wedding dua","nikkah dua","just married","newlywed"],t.s)
B.aPW=new A.aR(B.aeD,"The blessed wedding du'a: \"Barakallahu laka wa baraka 'alaika wa jama'a bainakuma fi khayr\" - May Allah bless you, shower blessings upon you, and join you both in goodness. (Sunan Abu Dawood 2130). And the house of the newlyweds is built upon five: gratitude, gentleness, patience, honesty, and prayer together.")
B.ahn=s(["new baby","newborn","baby born","child born","aqiqah","tahnik","baby"],t.s)
B.aOT=new A.aR(B.ahn,'For the newborn: give the adhan in the right ear and the iqamah in the left - the first voice it hears is the call to Allah. (Sunan Abu Dawood 5105). Tahnik: a softened date on the palate, and pray for the child. (Sahih al-Bukhari 5469). And the aqiqah: "Every child is pledged to its aqiqah" - an animal sacrificed on the seventh day, its weight in silver given as charity, and the child named. (Tirmidhi 1513)')
B.adI=s(["children","raising kids","my child","teaching children","kids behavior"],t.s)
B.aPo=new A.aR(B.adI,'"Every child is born upon the fitrah - the natural readiness for Islam; its parents make it a Jew, a Christian, or a Persian." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1385). Be the first kindness they know: the Prophet carried children, shortened the prayer when he heard a baby cry, and said: "He is not of us who does not have mercy on our young." (Tirmidhi 1919)')
B.aeF=s(["friday","jumuah","jumma","surah kahf","best hour friday"],t.s)
B.aP_=new A.aR(B.aeF,'Friday: purify and adorn, go early to the masjid, and leave trading aside when the call is made - "And when the prayer is concluded, disperse within the land and seek the bounty of Allah" (Al-Jumuah 9-10). The Prophet said Friday has an hour in which no Muslim happens to ask Allah for good but that He gives it - and it is believed to be the last hour after Asr. (Sahih al-Bukhari 935). Recite Surah al-Kahf: "a light between this Friday and the next." (Tirmidhi 2810)')
B.aoZ=s(["eid","eid dua","eid mubarak","eid salah"],t.s)
B.aOP=new A.aR(B.aoZ,'The Prophet said: "Every nation has its festival, and this is ours" - take a different route going and returning, praise Allah on the way, and embrace. (Sahih al-Bukhari 952). The takbeer: "Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, la ilaha illallah, wallahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar wa lillahil hamd" - aloud on the roads, softly in the heart.')
B.adN=s(["fasting shawwal","six days of shawwal","monday fasting","thursday fasting","white days","extra fasts","fast the year"],t.s)
B.aP7=new A.aR(B.adN,"Beyond Ramadan: fasting Ramadan then six days of Shawwal \"is like fasting the whole year\" (Sahih Muslim 1164). The Prophet fasted Mondays and Thursdays - deeds are presented on those days (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 747) - and the three white days, the 13th, 14th, and 15th of the lunar month (Tirmidhi 762). The most beloved fast to Allah is Dawud's: a day on, a day off. (Sahih al-Bukhari 3420)")
B.afI=s(["suhoor","sehri","pre-dawn meal"],t.s)
B.aQ_=new A.aR(B.afI,'"Take suhoor, for in suhoor there is blessing." (Sahih al-Bukhari 1923). Delay it toward dawn; the Prophet said the difference between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the pre-dawn meal. (Muslim 1096). Even dates and water carry the barakah.')
B.afh=s(["itikaf","spiritual retreat","last ten nights"],t.s)
B.aOY=new A.aR(B.afh,"I'tikaf - secluding oneself in the masjid for worship - was practiced by the Prophet every Ramadan, ten nights, and in the year he passed away, twenty. (Sahih al-Bukhari 2025). The minimum is a moment of intention in the masjid; the essence is to leave the world at the door and keep only conversation with Allah.")
B.aoO=s(["feed a fasting person","feeding iftar","iftar for someone","feed"],t.s)
B.aPz=new A.aR(B.aoO,"\"Whoever provides the food for a fasting person to break his fast earns the same reward as his, without the fasting person's reward being diminished in any way.\" (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 807). A date and a glass of milk suffice - and the angels make du'a for the giver all that evening.")
B.aaw=s(["rain dua","it's raining","rain blessing","rain shower","rain"],t.s)
B.aPc=new A.aR(B.aaw,'When the rain falls: "Allahumma sayyiban nafi\'an" - O Allah, make it a beneficial rain. (Sahih al-Bukhari 1032). And the downpour is an hour of answer: "Two are not rejected - the du\'a at the time of rain and the du\'a of the oppressed." (Abu Dawood 2540, Ibn Majah 3878). Expose some of it to the rain - it has newly come from its Lord.')
B.an1=s(["wind dua","storm dua","strong wind","thunder dua","lightning","wind","storm"],t.s)
B.aPS=new A.aR(B.an1,"For the wind: \"Allahumma inni as'aluka khayraha, wa khayra ma fiiha, wa khayra ma ursilat bihi, wa a'udhu bika min sharriha...\" - O Allah, I ask You for its good, the good in it, the good it was sent with, and I seek refuge in You from its evil. (Sahih Muslim 899). The thunder glorifies the praise of its Lord - say Subhan Allah as it rolls. (Musnad Ahmad)")
B.aji=s(["new moon","crescent moon","moon sighting","hilal","moon"],t.s)
B.aQc=new A.aR(B.aji,'Seeing the new crescent: "Allahumma ahillahu \'alaina bil amni wal iman, was-salamati wal islam..." - O Allah, let this moon rise over us with security, faith, safety, and Islam. (Sahih Muslim 1742). The sighting ties the ummah to the sky - the month begins when the crescent is seen, not when the calendar guesses.')
B.agb=s(["halal income","halal earnings","haram money","riba","interest","halal work","halal","haram"],t.s)
B.aOF=new A.aR(B.agb,'"O people, Allah is Pure and accepts only what is pure - He commands the believers as He commanded the messengers: eat of the good and do righteous work." (Sahih Muslim 1015). Earnings built on riba are fought by the Prophet himself: he cursed the one who consumes riba, the one who gives it, the one who records it, and its two witnesses - "they are alike." (Muslim 1598). Trade is blessed; the Prophet was a merchant and praised the honest trader.')
B.aiz=s(["gambling","lottery","betting","casino","poker"],t.s)
B.aPR=new A.aR(B.aiz,"\"O you who believe, intoxicants, gambling, idols, and divining arrows are but filth of Satan's handiwork - avoid it that you may succeed. Satan only intends to cause enmity and hatred between you through it and to bar you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer.\" (Al-Ma'idah 90-91). The money of gambling is built on taking without consent - the blessed exit door is always open.")
B.aaz=s(["alcohol","drinking","wine","beer","intoxicants"],t.s)
B.aPq=new A.aR(B.aaz,'"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every khamr is unlawful." (Sahih Muslim 2003) - and prayer is not accepted from one who is intoxicated for forty days if he does not repent. (Tirmidhi 3773). What poisons the mind is barred from the body, whatever shape the bottle takes.')
B.ajY=s(["eating manners","right hand eating","wash hands eating","table manners islam","eat","eating"],t.s)
B.aPv=new A.aR(B.ajY,'The Sunnah of the table: mention Allah\'s name, eat with the right hand, and eat from what is nearest - "If he forgets to mention Allah, let him say: Bismillahi awwalahu wa akhirahu." (Sahih Muslim 2017, 2020). Wash the hands before and after eating, for blessing descends when the hands are washed. (Sunan Abu Dawood 3755). Sit together - the shared meal is mercy and separation is from the shaytan. (Abu Dawood 3764)')
B.ajj=s(["miswak","tooth stick","brush teeth sunnah"],t.s)
B.aP5=new A.aR(B.ajj,'"Were it not that I might overburden my ummah, I would have commanded them to use the miswak before every prayer." (Sahih al-Bukhari 887). The Prophet cleaned his teeth at wudu, before prayer, before reciting, on waking - a different part of worship than fresh breath alone.')
B.aaQ=s(["honey","black seed","tibben nabawi","prophetic medicine","natural remedy"],t.s)
B.aQ9=new A.aR(B.aaQ,'From the Sunnah of healing: honey - "healing for the people" (An-Nahl 69), and the Prophet said healing is in three: the cut of the cupper, a drink of honey, and cauterization with fire - but he forbade his ummah cauterization. (Sahih al-Bukhari 5356). And black seed: "the healing for every disease except death" (Bukhari 5688). Medicine of the body and the ruqyah of the heart travel together.')
B.aos=s(["zamzam","drinking zamzam","umrah zamzam"],t.s)
B.aPQ=new A.aR(B.aos,'"The water of Zamzam is for whatever it is drunk for" - drink it with an intention: knowledge, healing, forgiveness, a righteous child. (Sunan Ibn Majah 3062). It sprang for Ismail in the desert of Makkah and has not ceased - five thousand years of answered thirst.')
B.amV=s(["cupping","hijamah","blood cupping"],t.s)
B.aOK=new A.aR(B.amV,"The Prophet praised cupping: \"The best of your treatments is hijamah\" - and had it done on the veins at the back of his neck, paying the cupper his wage. (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 1190). Even treatment has an etiquette: seek the skilled, pay fairly, and pair it with du'a.")
B.ad7=s(["cats","kittens","pet cat"],t.s)
B.aQ4=new A.aR(B.ad7,"Kindness to cats is from the Sunnah: a cat once slept on the Prophet's cloak; he cut the sleeve off rather than wake it when he stood for prayer - and he used its water for wudu. Cats are not impure, he said; they are among those who go about among you. (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 91). Muezza, they say, was the name of his own.")
B.ap_=s(["sleep dua","going to sleep","bedtime","sleep on right side","wake up dua","waking up","sleep"],t.s)
B.aPl=new A.aR(B.ap_,'Before sleep: wudu as you washed for prayer, lie on the right side, and recite Ayat al-Kursi - "a protector from Allah is appointed over you, and no devil comes near you until morning." (Sahih al-Bukhari 2311). Dust the bedding three times - "for you do not know what came to rest upon it." (Bukhari 6320). Waking: "Alhamdulillahilladhi ahyana ba\'da ma amatana wa ilaihin nushur" - all praise to Allah who gave us life after death, and to Him is the resurrection. (Bukhari 6312)')
B.ajT=s(["seeing someone sick","someone else afflicted","heard bad news"],t.s)
B.aOO=new A.aR(B.ajT,"When you see someone afflicted: \"Alhamdulillahil-ladhi 'afani mimabtalaaka bihi wa faddalani 'ala kathirin mimman khalaqa tafdila\" - praise to Allah who spared me what He afflicted you with and favored me over much of His creation. (Jami' at-Tirmidhi 3433). Gratitude without the afflicted hearing it; the reward and the mercy both remain.")
B.aeI=s(["someone died","death of a loved one","lost my mother","lost my father","grief","mourning","funeral","visiting graves","passed away","died","lost"],t.s)
B.aOH=new A.aR(B.aeI,'When death takes someone you love: "Inna lillahi wa inna ilaihi raji\'un - Allahumma\'jurni fi musibati wakhluf li khayran minha" - To Allah we belong and to Him we return; O Allah, reward me in my calamity and replace it for me with better. (Sahih Muslim 918). The Prophet said: "Allah says to the angels: build for My servant a palace in Paradise and call it the House of Praise." For the deceased: wash, shroud, pray over, and bury - attending carries the reward of two great qirats. (Bukhari 1325) And visit the graves - "they remind you of the Hereafter" (Muslim 977). Say to the grieving: "May Allah magnify your reward, beautify your patience, and forgive your departed."')
B.aec=s(["trust in allah","tawakkul","my rizq","provision","how will i survive","jobless","no money","money"],t.s)
B.aQd=new A.aR(B.aec,'The Prophet said: "If you relied upon Allah as He should be relied upon, He would provide for you as He provides for the birds - they leave in the morning with empty stomachs and return full." (Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 2344). And: "Tie your camel, then trust in Allah." (Tirmidhi 2517). Tawakkul is not the abandonment of means - it is the heart\'s grip on Allah while the hand grips the rope. Rizq was written when you were sixty days in the womb; what is yours will walk to you.')
B.ae5=s(["hurt myself","want to die","end my life","no point living","self harm","suicidal","don't want to live","kill myself","no will to live"],t.s)
B.aOB=new A.aR(B.ae5,'Please - stop, and breathe. Your pain is real, and so is Allah\'s promise: "Allah does not burden a soul beyond what it can bear" (Al-Baqarah 286), and "Despair not of the mercy of Allah" (Az-Zumar 53). This world can hurt unbearably, but the Prophet said: "No fatigue, nor illness, nor anxiety, nor sorrow, nor harm reaches a Muslim but that Allah expiates by it - even a thorn." (Sahih al-Bukhari 5641). You are not alone: the Prayer Times screen can connect you to a human near you, and Sakina is open whenever the night is heavy. Stay - the One who made you is not done with you.')
B.agV=s(["hijab","covering","modesty dress","why do muslim women cover"],t.s)
B.aPk=new A.aR(B.agV,'Allah says: "And tell the believing women to lower their gaze and guard their private parts and not expose their adornment except that which appears thereof, and to draw their coverings over their chests..." (An-Nur 31), and: "O Prophet, tell your wives and daughters and the women of the believers to draw their outer garments over themselves." (Al-Ahzab 59). The Prophet said that when a woman reaches menstruation, nothing should be seen of her but this and this - and he pointed to the face and hands. (Abu Dawood 4104) It is worship, obedience, and - for many who wear it - peace.')
B.ajU=s(["memorize quran","hifz","memorization tips","learn quran","quran study tips","memorize"],t.s)
B.aP6=new A.aR(B.ajU,'The memorizer\'s method, unchanged for a thousand years: a daily portion - new and revision - with recitation to a teacher who corrects. Ibn al-Jazari said: "Committing to what you can bear - even a little - is better than burning out on a lot." Recite in the same copy, at the same hour, and listen to one reciter only until the passage settles. The promise is sealed in the hadith: "The best of you are those who learn the Qur\'an and teach it." (Sahih al-Bukhari 5027)')
B.anL=s(["tajweed","pronunciation quran","recitation rules","makhraj"],t.s)
B.aQ0=new A.aR(B.anL,'Tajweed is giving every letter its right: from its makhraj - its exit point - and with its sifah - its characteristics - slowly, without artificiality. The Prophet listened to Ibn Umar\'s recitation for a long while and said: "Have mercy on yourself" - beautiful, unhurried recitation is loved. (Abu Dawood 802) Begin with one surah perfected; the Qur\'an itself teaches: "And recite the Qur\'an with measured recitation." (Al-Muzzammil 4)')
B.a8S=s(["learn arabic","arabic alphabet","arabic learning tips","arabic"],t.s)
B.aOU=new A.aR(B.a8S,"The alphabet is a door, not a mountain: twenty-nine letters, each with a shape at the start, middle, and end of a word. The Wasia Academy in this app walks children through every letter with sound and practice - and what works for them works for you: one letter a day, said aloud, written twice, found in a word you already know. Ten weeks of one letter a day, and the script that carried the revelation is yours.")
